<title>USA: UPS says strike will cost Teamsters' jobs.</title>
<headline>UPS says strike will cost Teamsters' jobs.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service chief executive officer James Kelly said Tuesday that the company will have 15,000 fewer Teamsters jobs if the strike continues for another two weeks.</p>
<p>&quot;We reviewed yesterday the impact of this strike after two weeks, after four weeks and after six months, and the conditions now are that we'll have 15,000 fewer Teamsters jobs if the strike ends in two weeks,&quot; he told NBC's &quot;Today&quot; show.</p>
</text>
